{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"3f78a678-bce9-4781-85d5-1464dbcdef21","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Cause\n\nNote pages (`/n/\u003cslug\u003e`) and the home page (`/`) serve the static shell [index.html](file:///tmp/h-DbwWmc/site/index.html) with `HTTP 200` and rely on [app.js](file:///tmp/h-DbwWmc/site/app.js#L6-L20) to fetch note content from `/v1/notes/\u003cslug\u003e` (and `/v1/notes?limit=50`).\n\nOn `2026-09-07`, `Disallow: /v1/` was added to [robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-DbwWmc/site/robots.txt) ([routes.md](file:///tmp/h-DbwWmc/api/routes.md#L14-L16)). When Googlebot renders a note page, it obeys `robots.txt` for subresource requests and blocks `fetch(\"/v1/notes/\u003cslug\u003e\")`. The rejected `fetch()` enters the `catch` block in [app.js](file:///tmp/h-DbwWmc/site/app.js#L18-L20), rendering:\n\n\u003e `NOT FOUND — No note lives at this address.`\n\nBecause the page returns `HTTP 200` while displaying a \"NOT FOUND\" message ([url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt](file:///tmp/h-DbwWmc/search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt)), Google classifies every page crawled after `2026-09-07` as a **Soft 404** ([pages-2026-10-16.csv](file:///tmp/h-DbwWmc/search-console/pages-2026-10-16.csv)).\n\n### Fix\n\n1. Updated [robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-DbwWmc/site/robots.txt) using Google's longest-match rule:\n   - Added `Allow: /v1/notes` so Googlebot can fetch `/v1/notes?limit=50` and `/v1/notes/{slug}`.\n   - Added `Disallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions` so the POST-only per-user reactions endpoint under `/v1/notes/` stays blocked (outmatching `Allow: /v1/notes`).\n   - Kept `Disallow: /v1/` and `Disallow: /admin/` so `/v1/me`, `/v1/me/drafts`, `/v1/auth/token`, and `/admin/` remain blocked.\n2. Documented the full root cause and rule evaluation in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-DbwWmc/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":161.418359,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":36657,"output_tokens":8395,"thinking_tokens":5099,"cache_read_tokens":136501,"total_tokens":45052}}}
